    {'para': '**424. Verbs. Root-class, cont’d.** ⟨ās⟩ ‘sit’ (mid.): Indic. ⟨āse⟩, ⟨āsse⟩, ⟨āste⟩; ⟨āsvahe⟩ etc.; ⟨āsmahe⟩, ⟨āddhve⟩∗, ⟨āsate⟩. Impf. ⟨āsi⟩, ⟨āsthās⟩, ⟨āsta⟩ etc. Imv. ⟨āsai⟩, ⟨āssva⟩, ⟨āstām⟩ etc. Part. ⟨āsīna⟩ (unique).'},
    {'para': '**425.** The root ⟨śās⟩, ‘command’ (act.), substitutes in the weak forms with consonant-endings the weakened stem ⟨śiṣ⟩; thus, indic. sing. ⟨śāsmi⟩ etc.; du. ⟨śiṣvas⟩ etc.; but 3rd pl. ⟨śāsati⟩. Impf.: ⟨aśāsam⟩, ⟨aśās⟩, ⟨aśāt⟩∗∗; ⟨aśiṣva⟩ etc.; but 3rd pl. ⟨aśāsus⟩. Imv. 2nd sing. ⟨śādhi⟩; 3rd pl. ⟨śāsatu⟩.'},
    {'para': '**426.** The extremely common root 1⟨as⟩, ‘be’ (act.), loses its vowel in weak forms, except when protected by the augment. The 2nd sing. imv. is ⟨edhi⟩; in the 2nd sing. indic. one ⟨s⟩ is omitted; in the 2nd and 3rd sing. impf. ⟨ī⟩ is inserted before the ending. Thus:'},
