    {'para': '**427.** Roots in ⟨h⟩ (except ⟨dih⟩ and ⟨duh⟩) combine ⟨h⟩ with ⟨t⟩, ⟨th⟩ and ⟨dh⟩ into ⟨ḍh⟩, and then lengthen preceding ⟨a⟩, ⟨i⟩, ⟨u⟩; before ⟨s⟩, ⟨h⟩ becomes ⟨k⟩; in 2nd and 3rd sing. impf. act. (where the endings are dropped) the ⟨h⟩ becomes ⟨ṭ⟩. Thus, ⟨lih⟩ ‘lick’ (act. and mid.): Impf. act.: ⟨aleham⟩, ⟨aleṭ⟩, ⟨aleṭ⟩; ⟨alihva⟩, ⟨alīḍham⟩,'},
