    {'para': '**429.** The roots ⟨rud⟩, ‘weep’, ⟨svap⟩, ‘sleep’, ⟨an⟩, ‘breathe’, ⟨śvas⟩, ‘breathe’ (all act.), insert ⟨i⟩ before all endings beginning with a consonant, except ⟨s⟩ and ⟨t⟩ of 2nd and 3rd sing. impf., where they insert either ⟨a⟩ or ⟨ī⟩. Thus, ⟨rud⟩: Pres. indic.: ⟨rodimi⟩, ⟨rodiṣi⟩ etc., 3rd pl. ⟨rudanti⟩. Impf.: ⟨arodam⟩, ⟨arodīs⟩ or ⟨arodas⟩, ⟨arodīt⟩ or ⟨arodat⟩; ⟨arudiva⟩ etc.; 3rd pl. ⟨arudan⟩. Imv.: ⟨rodāni⟩, ⟨rudihi⟩, ⟨roditu⟩ etc. Opt.: ⟨rudyām⟩ etc. (⟨yā⟩ being mode-sign).'},
